# https://qdrant.tech/
## Overall Summary
> Qdrant is an Open-Source Vector Search Engine written in Rust. It provides fast and scalable vector similarity search service with convenient API.

## Documentation
- [Qdrant Fundamentals](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/faq/qdrant-fundamentals/index.md): Common questions about Qdrant fundamentals — vector dimensions, payload limits, multivectors, real-time updates, and how similarity search behaves at scale.
- [Reranking for Better Search](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/search-precision/reranking-semantic-search/index.md): Improve semantic search and RAG quality in Qdrant by adding a reranking stage that re-scores top candidates with a cross-encoder for higher-precision results.
- [Text Filtering](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/search/text-search/text-filtering/index.md): Apply keyword and text filters in Qdrant to narrow down search results by exact string values, multiple authors, or full-text terms — including progressive filtering via the batch search API.
- [Database Optimization](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/faq/database-optimization/index.md): FAQ on optimizing Qdrant: cut memory with quantization and on-disk storage, size machines correctly, and diagnose slow queries with payload indexing.
- [Full-Text Search](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/search/text-search/full-text-search/index.md): Use Qdrant's sparse vector support to perform full-text search with BM25, SPLADE++, and miniCOIL — including language-specific settings and parameter tuning.
- [Multivectors and Late Interaction](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-search-engineering/using-multivector-representations/index.md): Tutorial: use Qdrant multivectors with late interaction reranking to capture token-level signals and improve precision while controlling RAM and indexing cost.
- [Relevance Feedback Retrieval in Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-search-engineering/using-relevance-feedback/index.md): Tutorial: integrate Qdrant's relevance feedback query into a search pipeline, customize feedback parameters, and evaluate retrieval quality gains.
- [Collaborative Filtering](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-search-engineering/collaborative-filtering/index.md): Build an effective movie recommendation system using collaborative filtering and Qdrant's similarity search.
- [Hugging Face Dataset Ingestion](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-basics/huggingface-datasets/index.md): Step-by-step guide to ingest Hugging Face datasets into Qdrant collections using the Python SDK, with batching and streaming for large vector workloads.
- [Hybrid Search](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/search/text-search/hybrid-search/index.md): Build hybrid search pipelines in Qdrant by combining dense semantic vectors and sparse lexical vectors with the prefetch API and Reciprocal Rank Fusion for comprehensive search results.
- [Async API](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-develop/async-api/index.md): Tutorial: use Qdrant's async Python API with FastAPI and other ASGI frameworks to build non-blocking, high-throughput vector search applications.
- [Multivector Document Retrieval](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-search-engineering/pdf-retrieval-at-scale/index.md): Optimizing PDF retrieval at scale with Qdrant and Vision Large Language Models (VLLMs) such as ColPali and ColQwen. Two-stage retrieval with multivector representations mean pooling.
- [Agentic RAG with CrewAI](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-build-essentials/agentic-rag-crewai-zoom/index.md): Step-by-step tutorial: build an agentic RAG system with Qdrant and CrewAI to store, retrieve, and analyze meeting transcripts through coordinated AI agents.
- [Configuration](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/ops-configuration/configuration/index.md): Configure Qdrant via config files and environment variables to set storage paths, network interfaces, performance parameters, and feature flags.
- [Create a Cluster](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud/create-cluster/index.md): Create a free or standard Qdrant Cloud cluster on AWS, GCP, or Azure, with high availability, GPU acceleration, and Hybrid Cloud deployment options.
- [Databricks Ingestion](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/send-data/databricks/index.md): Generate dense and sparse embeddings on Databricks with Spark and load them into Qdrant using the Spark connector for scalable vector ingestion pipelines.
- [From Pinecone](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-pinecone/index.md): Migrate from Pinecone to Qdrant by streaming serverless index data, vectors, namespaces, and metadata into Qdrant collections with the Qdrant Migration Tool.
- [GraphRAG with Qdrant and Neo4j](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/graphrag-qdrant-neo4j/index.md): A step-by-step guide on implementing GraphRAG with Qdrant and Neo4j, combining vector search with knowledge graphs for enhanced retrieval.
- [Keeping Postgres and Qdrant in Sync](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-synchronization/with-postgres/index.md): Sync Postgres with Qdrant using dual-write, queued, or Change Data Capture patterns to keep vector search aligned with your relational source of truth.
- [Measuring ANN Recall](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-search-engineering/ann-recall/index.md): Measuring ANN Recall Time: 15 min Level: Beginner This tutorial focuses on ANN recall: how closely approximate nearest-neighbor (ANN) search matches exact kNN search, measured with recall@k.
- [Monitoring & Telemetry](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/ops-monitoring/monitoring/index.md): Scrape Qdrant metrics in Prometheus and OpenMetrics format and visualize cluster, collection, and node-level telemetry in Grafana monitoring dashboards.
- [OpenLLMetry](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/observability/openllmetry/index.md): Instrument the Qdrant client with OpenLLMetry, an OpenTelemetry-based observability layer from Traceloop, and export traces to any OTel-compatible backend.
- [Optimize Performance](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/ops-optimization/optimize/index.md): Optimize Qdrant performance with quantization, on-disk vector storage, and HNSW tuning to balance search speed, precision, and memory consumption.
- [Points](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/manage-data/points/index.md): Manage points in Qdrant collections by upserting, updating, deleting, and retrieving records that combine a vector with an optional JSON payload for search.
- [Pre-Migration Baseline](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migration-guidance/pre-migration-baseline/index.md): Record a pre-migration baseline of collection inventory, metadata schema, and reference search results so you can verify a clean migration cutover to Qdrant.
- [Pulumi](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud-tools/pulumi/index.md): Use Pulumi to provision and manage Qdrant Cloud clusters as code, defining clusters, API keys, and packages in Python, TypeScript, Go, or other supported languages.
- [Role Management](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud-rbac/role-management/index.md): Create, edit, and assign custom Qdrant Cloud roles with fine-grained permissions, or use built-in Base, Admin, and Owner roles for access control.
- [Search](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/search/search/index.md): Run similarity search in Qdrant to retrieve nearest-neighbor points for text, image, and multimodal queries using configurable distance metrics and HNSW.
- [Setup Hybrid Cloud](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/hybrid-cloud/hybrid-cloud-setup/index.md): Onboard a Kubernetes cluster as a Qdrant Hybrid Cloud Environment by installing the Operator and Cloud Agent with the required storage and permissions.
- [Setup Private Cloud](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/private-cloud/private-cloud-setup/index.md): Install Qdrant Private Cloud into any standard Kubernetes cluster with Helm, the Qdrant Operator, and credentials for the Qdrant container registry.
- [Vertical Scaling](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/scaling/vertical-scaling/index.md): Learn when and how to scale Qdrant vertically by resizing node resources, including RAM sizing formulas, Qdrant Cloud and self-hosted resize steps, and the signals that mean it's time to scale horizontally instead.
- [What is Qdrant?](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/overview/what-is-qdrant/index.md): Qdrant is a vector database for storing, searching, and managing high-dimensional embeddings — purpose-built for semantic search, RAG, and recommendations.
- [Measuring Retrieval Relevance](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/improve-search/retrieval-relevance/index.md): Measuring Retrieval Relevance Time: 40 min Level: Intermediate This tutorial focuses on retrieval relevance: how well retrieved results match real user intent. To measure retrieval relevance, you need
- [Evaluating Pipeline Output Quality](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/improve-search/pipeline-output-quality/index.md): Evaluating Pipeline Output Quality Time: 45 min Level: Intermediate This tutorial focuses on pipeline output quality: whether the full retrieval pipeline produces the right output once retrieved
- [Memory Usage](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/ops-monitoring/memory-usage/index.md): Use the Qdrant Web UI or API to monitor a collection's disk, RAM, and page cache consumption across the cluster and per component, to plan capacity and diagnose memory pressure.
- [Resource Quotas](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/ops-configuration/quotas/index.md): Configure cluster-wide memory and disk quotas in Qdrant, understand HTTP 507 rejections and replica deactivation, and find which node in a cluster is full.
- [Query Decomposition for Multi-Hop Questions](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/improve-search/query-decomposition/index.md): Answer multi-hop questions in Qdrant: decompose the query into retrieval steps, let an LLM ask each follow-up, and fuse results with RRF.
- [Slow Request Log](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/ops-monitoring/slow-request-log/index.md): Use the Slow Request Log REST endpoint to find which queries are responsible for high latency, with per-request-type breakdowns, deduplication by request content, and approximate occurrence counts.
- [Administration](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/ops-configuration/administration/index.md): Manage Qdrant at runtime with administration tools for recovery mode, strict mode, and guardrails against expensive queries on unindexed payload fields.
- [Authentication](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud/authentication/index.md): Create Qdrant Cloud Database API keys with granular access control, configure expirations, and authenticate to your clusters with best-practice rotation.
- [Configuration](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/private-cloud/configuration/index.md): Configure the Qdrant Private Cloud Helm chart with Operator settings, networking, scheduling, ingress, and backup management options for Kubernetes.
- [Create a Cluster](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/hybrid-cloud/hybrid-cloud-cluster-creation/index.md): Create a production-ready Qdrant cluster in Hybrid Cloud with Kubernetes scheduling controls, node selectors, and secret-based API key authentication.
- [Data Integrity](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migration-guidance/data-integrity/index.md): Run data integrity checks after migrating to Qdrant by comparing vector counts, sample records, and payload fields against your source vector database.
- [Filtering](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/search/filtering/index.md): Filter Qdrant search results with payload conditions on metadata and IDs, combining database-style clauses with vector similarity for precise retrieval.
- [From Weaviate](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-weaviate/index.md): Migrate from Weaviate to Qdrant by streaming classes, vectors, and properties into Qdrant collections using the Qdrant Migration Tool's Weaviate connector.
- [Horizontal Scaling](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/scaling/horizontal-scaling/index.md): Learn how Qdrant's distributed model works: sharding, the default replication behavior, Raft consensus for cluster metadata, and the consistency trade-off.
- [Inference API](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/inference/inference-api/index.md): Inference API When using Qdrant Cloud Inference or Qdrant&amp;rsquo;s BM25 model, embeddings are generated server-side. Instead of pre-computed vectors, you pass Inference Objects when ingesting or
- [LLM-Powered Filter Automation](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/search-precision/automate-filtering-with-llms/index.md): Automate filter construction in Qdrant by using an LLM to convert natural-language queries into structured payload filter conditions for precise vector search.
- [Managed Cloud Prometheus Monitoring](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/ops-monitoring/managed-cloud-prometheus/index.md): Configure Prometheus and Grafana in Kubernetes to scrape metrics from Qdrant Managed Cloud clusters and import the official monitoring dashboard.
- [OpenLIT](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/observability/openlit/index.md): Use OpenLIT, an OpenTelemetry-native LLM observability tool, to auto-instrument Qdrant and forward traces and metrics to your existing telemetry backend.
- [Optimizer](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/ops-optimization/optimizer/index.md): See how Qdrant's background optimizer reclaims deleted points, merges segments, and rebuilds indexes to keep storage compact and search performance high.
- [Querying with Airflow](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/send-data/qdrant-airflow-astronomer/index.md): Build Apache Airflow DAGs on Astronomer that generate embeddings in parallel and run semantic queries against Qdrant for production data pipelines.
- [Quickstart](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/edge/edge-quickstart/index.md): Set up Qdrant Edge with Python or Rust bindings to configure shards, upsert points, build payload indexes, and run local vector search on-device.
- [Quickstart](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/fastembed/fastembed-quickstart/index.md): Install FastEmbed, load a default text embedding model, and generate vectors from sample documents in this quickstart for Qdrant's lightweight embedding library.
- [S3 Ingestion with LangChain](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-build-essentials/data-ingestion-beginners/index.md): Tutorial: build a data ingestion pipeline that pulls documents from AWS S3, generates embeddings via LangChain, and stores them in Qdrant for semantic search.
- [Semantic Search 101](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-basics/search-beginners/index.md): Step-by-step tutorial: spin up a Qdrant Cloud cluster, create a collection, upload sample data, and run semantic vector search queries in five minutes.
- [Shard Lifecycle](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/edge/edge-api/shard-lifecycle/index.md): Reference for the Qdrant Edge Shard lifecycle methods: creating a new shard, loading an existing one, inspecting its path and configuration, reading shard metadata with info, flushing to disk, and closing it.
- [Snapshots](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-operations/create-snapshot/index.md): Tutorial: create, download, and restore Qdrant snapshots to back up collections or migrate data between single-node and distributed multi-node clusters.
- [Terraform](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud-tools/terraform/index.md): Provision Qdrant Cloud clusters and database keys with the official Terraform provider to manage vector database infrastructure as code on AWS, GCP, and Azure.
- [Understanding Vector Search in Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/overview/vector-search/index.md): Learn how vector search uses embeddings to retrieve by semantic meaning, how it differs from keyword search, and where Qdrant fits in the retrieval stack.
- [User Management](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud-rbac/user-management/index.md): Invite teammates, assign or revoke roles, transfer account ownership, and remove users from your Qdrant Cloud account through User Management.
- [Vectors](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/manage-data/vectors/index.md): Define dense, sparse, and multivector configurations in Qdrant collections to support text, image, multimodal, and late-interaction retrieval like ColBERT.
- [Multi-Representation Search](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-search-engineering/multi-representation-search/index.md): Multi-Representation Search Across Titles, Abstracts, and Chunks Time: 45 min Level: Intermediate Output: GitHub A document is rarely well-represented by a single embedding. A paper has a title, an
- [Branch-Aware Search](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-search-engineering/branch-aware-search/index.md): Index a versioned document corpus in Qdrant and scope each query to one branch's live view by walking its lineage with a payload filter.
- [Memory Tiers](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/ops-configuration/memory-tiers/index.md): Learn how Qdrant's memory parameter (cold, cached, pinned) controls RAM residency for vectors, indexes, quantized data, and payloads.
- [Indexing Payloads of Random Shape](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-search-engineering/index-dynamic-payloads/index.md): Model payloads with arbitrary keys in Qdrant. Reshape open-ended fields into a key-value array, index it at setup, and query exact matches and ranges with a nested filter.
- [Compressed Multivector Search](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-search-engineering/turbo4-multivector-search/index.md): Store multivector late interaction embeddings with Qdrant's turbo4 datatype and query them alongside dense and sparse vectors.
- [Agentic RAG with LangGraph](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-build-essentials/agentic-rag-langgraph/index.md): Tutorial: build an agentic RAG workflow using LangGraph for state management and Qdrant for vector retrieval, with multi-source routing and tool orchestration.
- [Cluster Access](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud/cluster-access/index.md): Access Qdrant Cloud clusters through the integrated UI, REST and gRPC APIs, node-specific endpoints, and IP allowlists for restricted network access.
- [Configure, Scale & Update Clusters](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/hybrid-cloud/configure-scale-upgrade/index.md): Configure, scale horizontally or vertically, reshard, and upgrade Qdrant Hybrid Cloud clusters with automatic shard rebalancing on Kubernetes.
- [From Milvus](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-milvus/index.md): Migrate from Milvus or Zilliz Cloud to Qdrant by streaming vectors, payloads, and metadata from Milvus collections into Qdrant with the Qdrant Migration Tool.
- [Hybrid Queries](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/search/hybrid-queries/index.md): Run hybrid queries in Qdrant: fuse dense, sparse, and multivector results with RRF or DBSF, layer custom scoring with Formula Query, and pick the right method for your data.
- [Kafka Streaming into Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/send-data/data-streaming-kafka-qdrant/index.md): Build real-time CDC pipelines that stream data from Kafka and Confluent into Qdrant, enabling fresh semantic search and retrieval-augmented generation.
- [Managing a Cluster](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/private-cloud/qdrant-cluster-management/index.md): Manage Qdrant Private Cloud clusters declaratively in Kubernetes to scale resources, upgrade Qdrant versions, and expose clusters via Service or Ingress.
- [On-Device Embeddings](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/edge/edge-fastembed-embeddings/index.md): Pair FastEmbed with Qdrant Edge to generate text and image embeddings on-device, enabling fully offline vector search with cached local models.
- [Payload](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/manage-data/payload/index.md): Store JSON payloads alongside vectors in Qdrant, then use them for filtering, faceting, and result ranking to combine metadata with semantic similarity search.
- [Permission Reference](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud-rbac/permission-reference/index.md): Browse the full list of Qdrant Cloud RBAC permissions covering identity, clusters, API keys, backups, Hybrid Cloud, billing, and account management.
- [Read-Write Contention](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/ops-optimization/read-write-contention/index.md): A step-by-step guide to reducing read-write contention in Qdrant when the background optimizer competes with search queries under continuous write load.
- [Resilience](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/scaling/resilience/index.md): Learn how replication factor and node count together determine Qdrant's fault tolerance, how Multi-AZ differs from replication, and how to configure failover for production.
- [Search Quality](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migration-guidance/search-quality/index.md): Validate search quality after migrating to Qdrant using tiered checks that compare ranking, recall, and filter behavior against your source vector database.
- [Self-Hosted Prometheus Monitoring](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/ops-monitoring/hybrid-cloud-prometheus/index.md): Set up Prometheus and Grafana in Kubernetes to scrape metrics from Qdrant Hybrid Cloud and Private Cloud databases for end-to-end observability.
- [Usage Statistics](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/ops-configuration/usage-statistics/index.md): Review what anonymized telemetry the Qdrant open-source container collects, how the data is anonymized, and how to deactivate or request deletion.
- [BM25](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/edge/edge-bm25/index.md): Use the built-in BM25 embedder in Qdrant Edge to generate sparse text embeddings on-device for keyword search, without an internet connection or external model server.
- [Backups](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/private-cloud/backups/index.md): Back up and restore Qdrant Private Cloud clusters with one-time snapshots, recurring scheduled backups, and declarative Kubernetes restore resources.
- [BM25](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/inference/inference-bm25/index.md): Server-side Inference: BM25 BM25 (Best Matching 25) is a ranking function for text search. BM25 uses sparse vectors that represent documents, where each dimension corresponds to a word. Qdrant can
- [Building a Chain-of-Thought Medical Chatbot with Qdrant and DSPy](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/qdrant-dspy-medicalbot/index.md): Build a chain-of-thought medical chatbot with Qdrant and DSPy using RAG, dense embeddings, and ColBERT multivectors for accurate, citation-backed answers.
- [Collections](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/manage-data/collections/index.md): Configure Qdrant collections, define named vectors with configurable distance metrics, and manage the building blocks of vector search at the collection level.
- [Configuration](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/edge/edge-api/configuration/index.md): Reference for Qdrant Edge configuration: EdgeConfig, dense and sparse vector parameters, optimizer settings and the optimize method, WAL options, and changing configuration on a live shard.
- [Configure the Qdrant Operator](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/hybrid-cloud/operator-configuration/index.md): Tune the Qdrant Operator in Hybrid Cloud with advanced options for scheduling, security, ingress, networking, and automated snapshot management.
- [Data Migration](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-operations/migration/index.md): Tutorial: use the Qdrant Migration Tool to stream vectors from Pinecone, Weaviate, Chroma, or another Qdrant cluster with resumable, live migrations.
- [Data Synchronization Patterns](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/edge/edge-data-synchronization-patterns/index.md): Synchronize Qdrant Edge Shards with server collections through snapshots, partial updates, and dual-write patterns for offline-first edge applications.
- [Diagnosing Discrepancies](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migration-guidance/diagnosing-discrepancies/index.md): Diagnose post-migration discrepancies in Qdrant by separating data-level issues from configuration drift in indexing, scoring, and filtering behavior.
- [Discord RAG Bot](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-build-essentials/agentic-rag-camelai-discord/index.md): Tutorial: build an agentic RAG Discord bot that uses Qdrant for vector retrieval, CAMEL-AI agents for reasoning, and OpenAI embeddings for context-aware replies.
- [Distributed Deployment](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/scaling/distributed_deployment/index.md): Configure distributed Qdrant deployments to scale storage, balance load, and tolerate node failures using sharding and replication across a cluster.
- [Explore](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/search/explore/index.md): Use Qdrant's exploration APIs for recommendation, discovery, and dissimilar-vector search to power data discovery, cleaning, and personalized retrieval.
- [FastEmbed & Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/fastembed/fastembed-semantic-search/index.md): Use Qdrant Client with FastEmbed to build end-to-end semantic search: generate embeddings, create a collection, and query for the most relevant documents.
- [From Elasticsearch](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-elasticsearch/index.md): Migrate from Elasticsearch to Qdrant by streaming vector indexes, source documents, and metadata into Qdrant collections with the Qdrant Migration Tool.
- [Monitoring with Datadog](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/ops-monitoring/hybrid-cloud-datadog/index.md): Set up the Datadog Operator in Kubernetes to scrape Qdrant metrics from Hybrid Cloud and Private Cloud clusters using OpenMetrics, and visualize them in Datadog.
- [Running with GPU](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/ops-configuration/running-with-gpu/index.md): Enable GPU-accelerated vector indexing in Qdrant with dedicated Docker images for NVIDIA and AMD hardware, powered by the Vulkan compute API.
- [Scale Clusters](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud/cluster-scaling/index.md): Scale Qdrant Cloud clusters vertically or horizontally with automatic shard rebalancing to match growing vector data volumes and query workloads.
- [Semantic Search for Code](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-develop/code-search/index.md): Tutorial: build a semantic code search engine with Qdrant by combining natural-language and code-specific embeddings to navigate large source codebases.
- [Consistency Guarantees](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/scaling/consistency-guarantees/index.md): Configure Qdrant's consistency guarantees: the write consistency factor, read consistency levels, and write ordering options, with API examples in every client library.
- [Configure Clusters](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud/configure-cluster/index.md): Configure Qdrant Cloud clusters with collection defaults, strict mode, replication factors, and advanced optimizer settings tailored to your workload.
- [From OpenSearch](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-opensearch/index.md): Migrate from OpenSearch to Qdrant by streaming k-NN indexes, vectors, and document payloads into Qdrant collections with the Qdrant Migration Tool's connector.
- [Logging & Monitoring](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/private-cloud/logging-monitoring/index.md): Collect application logs and audit logs and scrape Prometheus-compatible metrics from Qdrant Private Cloud clusters, with a ready-made Grafana dashboard.
- [Multimodal Search](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-basics/multimodal-search/index.md): Combine Cohere Embed 4.0 with Qdrant Cloud Inference to power multimodal, multilingual vector search application over images and text using a shared embedding space.
- [Multitenancy with LlamaIndex](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/llama-index-multitenancy/index.md): Configure multitenant retrieval with LlamaIndex and Qdrant via payload-based partitioning, isolating per-user data in a single shared collection.
- [Networking, Logging & Monitoring](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/hybrid-cloud/networking-logging-monitoring/index.md): Configure network policies, log collection, and Prometheus-compatible metrics for Qdrant Hybrid Cloud, and visualize cluster health in Grafana.
- [Node Failure Recovery](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/scaling/node-failure-recovery/index.md): Step-by-step recovery procedures for Qdrant node failures: restarting with replicated collections, recreating a failed node, and recovering from a snapshot when no replicas remain.
- [Storage](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/manage-data/storage/index.md): Configure Qdrant storage across segments, balancing in-memory, memory-mapped, and on-disk options for vectors and payloads to fit cost and latency goals.
- [From Azure AI Search](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-azure-search/index.md): Migrate from Azure AI Search to Qdrant by streaming vectors and retrievable document fields into Qdrant collections, recreating vector dimensions and distance metrics with the Qdrant Migration Tool's connector.
- [5-Minute RAG with DeepSeek](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-build-essentials/rag-deepseek/index.md): Step-by-step tutorial: build a RAG pipeline with Qdrant and DeepSeek that stores embeddings in a vector database and grounds LLM answers in retrieved context.
- [API Reference](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/private-cloud/api-reference/index.md): Browse the Qdrant Private Cloud Kubernetes API reference for clusters, snapshots, restores, scheduled backups, and authentication custom resources.
- [Build a Semantic Search API](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-develop/neural-search/index.md): Tutorial: build a neural search service that encodes text with sentence transformers, indexes vectors in Qdrant, and serves results through FastAPI.
- [Cloud Inference](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/inference/cloud-inference/index.md): Qdrant Cloud Inference Clusters on Qdrant Managed Cloud can use Qdrant Cloud Inference to generate embeddings. For a list of available models and their dimensions, visit the Inference tab of the
- [Deployment Platforms](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/hybrid-cloud/platform-deployment-options/index.md): Deploy Qdrant Hybrid Cloud on managed Kubernetes platforms such as AWS EKS, GCP GKE, Azure AKS, and Linode LKE with platform-specific guidance.
- [From pgvector](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-pgvector/index.md): Migrate from pgvector to Qdrant by streaming rows from Postgres tables into Qdrant collections for scalable vector search with payload filtering and sharding.
- [Indexing](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/manage-data/indexing/index.md): Configure HNSW vector indexes and payload indexes in Qdrant to accelerate similarity search with filters on structured fields and high-cardinality metadata.
- [Migrate to a New Embedding Model](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-operations/embedding-model-migration/index.md): Tutorial: switch embedding models in Qdrant with zero downtime by running a blue-green migration across two collections while serving live traffic.
- [Monitor Clusters](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud/cluster-monitoring/index.md): Track Qdrant Cloud cluster health through metrics, logs, and automated email alerts that flag memory pressure, disk usage, and availability problems.
- [Optimize Throughput](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/fastembed/fastembed-optimize/index.md): Optimize FastEmbed throughput by parallelizing embedding workers, batching documents, and enabling GPU acceleration for high-volume indexing pipelines.
- [Private Chatbot for Interactive Learning](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/rag-chatbot-red-hat-openshift-haystack/index.md): Deploy a private RAG chatbot on Red Hat OpenShift with Qdrant Hybrid Cloud and Haystack, keeping training content and queries inside your infrastructure.
- [Search Relevance](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/search/search-relevance/index.md): Tune search relevance in Qdrant by adjusting scoring, applying payload-based ranking, and incorporating business signals to reorder vector search results.
- [Synchronize with a Server](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/edge/edge-synchronization-guide/index.md): Combine mutable and immutable Qdrant Edge Shards with a central server to offload indexing, back up data, and keep multiple edge devices in sync.
- [Updating Data](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/edge/edge-api/updating-data/index.md): Reference for updating data in a Qdrant Edge Shard: the update method, every UpdateOperation constructor in Python, and the equivalent Rust enum variants.
- [Incremental Embedding Updates](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-operations/incremental-embedding-updates/index.md): Keep embeddings in the Qdrant search engine in sync with documentation that changes over time, for up-to-date vector search.
- [Prevent Unoptimized Usage](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-operations/prevent-unoptimized-usage/index.md): Use the prevent_unoptimized optimizer setting to stop bulk uploads and config changes from slowing down search, and see what it costs in recall.
- [Blue-Green Cluster Deployment](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-operations/blue-green-deployment/index.md): Tutorial: use a blue-green cluster deployment to perform version upgrades, dataset refreshes, or resharding on Qdrant without risking production downtime.
- [Changelog](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/private-cloud/changelog/index.md): Track Qdrant Private Cloud releases, supported Qdrant versions, new features, performance improvements, and stability fixes across versions.
- [From S3 Vectors](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-s3-vectors/index.md): Migrate from S3 Vectors to Qdrant by streaming vectors, metadata, and indexes out of S3 Vectors into Qdrant collections with the Qdrant Migration Tool.
- [Implement Cohere RAG connector](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/cohere-rag-connector/index.md): Build a Cohere RAG connector over Qdrant, indexing data with Cohere embeddings and serving it to Command-R for grounded, citation-aware responses.
- [Low-Latency Search](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/search/low-latency-search/index.md): Reduce Qdrant search latency by tuning HNSW indexes, quantization, sharding, and replica routing for fast vector retrieval in distributed deployments.
- [n8n Workflow Automation](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-build-essentials/qdrant-n8n/index.md): Tutorial: connect Qdrant to n8n to automate vector search, recommendations, and unstructured data workflows using a low-code visual pipeline builder.
- [Quantization](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/manage-data/quantization/index.md): Apply quantization in Qdrant to compress high-dimensional vectors, reduce memory footprint, and accelerate similarity search while preserving recall quality.
- [Time-Based Sharding](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-operations/time-based-sharding/index.md): Tutorial: configure time-based sharding in Qdrant to route data by timestamp, target queries to recent shards, and prune older data without re-indexing.
- [Update Clusters](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud/cluster-upgrades/index.md): Upgrade Qdrant Cloud clusters to new versions through the console, with rolling zero-downtime updates on multi-node clusters that use replication.
- [Backup Clusters](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud/backups/index.md): Set up scheduled snapshots, on-demand backups, and one-click restores for Qdrant Cloud clusters to protect against data loss and enable disaster recovery.
- [External Providers](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/inference/external-inference-providers/index.md): External Embedding Model Providers Qdrant Cloud can act as a proxy for the APIs of external embedding model providers: OpenAI Cohere Jina AI OpenRouter This enables you to access any of the embedding
- [From Chroma](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-chroma/index.md): Migrate from Chroma to Qdrant by streaming collections, vectors, and metadata into a Qdrant cluster using the Qdrant Migration Tool's Chroma source connector.
- [Hybrid Search](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-basics/cloud-inference-hybrid-search/index.md): Build a hybrid search engine on Qdrant Cloud that fuses dense embeddings with BM25 sparse vectors using reciprocal rank fusion for higher-precision retrieval.
- [Large-Scale Search](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-operations/large-scale-search/index.md): Tutorial: index and search hundreds of millions of vectors in Qdrant on minimal hardware while keeping search latency and accuracy production-grade.
- [Multitenancy](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/manage-data/multitenancy/index.md): Set up Qdrant multitenancy with payload-based partitioning and per-tenant indexes for tenant isolation, predictable performance, and lower cluster overhead.
- [Question-Answering System for AI Customer Support](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/rag-customer-support-cohere-airbyte-aws/index.md): Set up a private customer-support RAG pipeline on AWS with Qdrant Hybrid Cloud, Cohere models, and Airbyte ingestion for continuous, secure data sync.
- [Reading Data](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/edge/edge-api/reading-data/index.md): Reference for reading data from a Qdrant Edge Shard: similarity search with query, paging with scroll, grouping, retrieving points by ID, counting, and faceting payload fields.
- [Video Anomaly Detection Part 1: Architecture, Twelve Labs, and NVIDIA VSS](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-build-essentials/video-anomaly-edge-part-1/index.md): Part 1 tutorial: design a real-time video anomaly detection pipeline using Qdrant Edge vector search, Twelve Labs embeddings, and NVIDIA Metropolis VSS.
- [Working with miniCOIL](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/fastembed/fastembed-minicoil/index.md): Use miniCOIL with FastEmbed and Qdrant for sparse neural retrieval that combines BM25-style keyword matching with contextual semantic ranking.
- [GPU-Accelerated HNSW Indexing](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-operations/gpu-accelerated-hnsw-indexing/index.md): Build a GPU-powered Qdrant Cloud cluster, measure how GPU acceleration affects HNSW indexing time and query latency, and compare cost against a CPU-only cluster.
- [Bulk Upload](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/manage-data/bulk-upload/index.md): A practical guide to bulk-uploading vectors into Qdrant: batch and parallelize uploads, create multiple shards, set up payload indexes before ingestion, store large datasets directly on disk with memmap, and mitigate read-write contention during continuous ingestion.
- [Chat With Product PDF Manuals Using Hybrid Search](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/hybrid-search-llamaindex-jinaai/index.md): Create a RAG chatbot for PDF manuals using Qdrant Hybrid Cloud, LlamaIndex, and Jina embeddings, with hybrid search for precise customer-support answers.
- [Inference](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud/inference/index.md): Generate dense, sparse, and multimodal embeddings inside Qdrant Cloud, or proxy requests to OpenAI, Cohere, and Jina without managing inference servers.
- [Secure a Self-Hosted Qdrant Instance](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-operations/secure-qdrant/index.md): Tutorial: secure a self-hosted Qdrant instance step by step: enable TLS, set up an Admin API key, restrict consumers with a Read-Only key, and issue collection-scoped JWT tokens.
- [Video Anomaly Detection Part 2: Edge-to-Cloud Pipeline](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-build-essentials/video-anomaly-edge-part-2/index.md): Part 2 tutorial: implement the edge-to-cloud pipeline for video anomaly detection with Qdrant Edge shards, snapshot sync, and offline-ready vector search.
- [Build a Hybrid Search API](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-develop/hybrid-search-fastembed/index.md): Tutorial: build a hybrid search API with Qdrant and FastEmbed that fuses dense and sparse embeddings, served through a FastAPI application.
- [Matryoshka Models](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/inference/matryoshka-models/index.md): Reduce Vector Dimensionality with Matryoshka Models Matryoshka Representation Learning (MRL) is a technique used to train embedding models to produce vectors that can be reduced in size with minimal
- [Region-Specific Contract Management System](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/rag-contract-management-stackit-aleph-alpha/index.md): Deploy a contract management RAG application on STACKIT with Qdrant Hybrid Cloud and Aleph Alpha embeddings and LLMs for region-restricted document search.
- [Video Anomaly Detection Part 3: Scoring, Governance, and Deployment](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-build-essentials/video-anomaly-edge-part-3/index.md): Part 3 tutorial: turn raw kNN scores into incidents, protect the baseline, and deploy a Qdrant Edge video anomaly detection system to production.
- [Working with SPLADE](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/fastembed/fastembed-splade/index.md): Use SPLADE with FastEmbed to produce sparse text embeddings for Qdrant, enabling interpretable, large-scale retrieval that improves on BM25-style ranking.
- [RAG System for Employee Onboarding](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/natural-language-search-oracle-cloud-infrastructure-cohere-langchain/index.md): Build a private onboarding RAG system on Oracle Cloud with Qdrant Hybrid Cloud, Cohere, and LangChain for natural-language search over internal documents.
- [Hybrid Search with Reranking](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-basics/reranking-hybrid-search/index.md): Step-by-step tutorial: build hybrid search in Qdrant combining dense, sparse, and late-interaction reranking for higher precision on large corpora.
- [Private RAG Information Extraction Engine](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/rag-chatbot-vultr-dspy-ollama/index.md): Build a private RAG information-extraction pipeline on Vultr using Qdrant Hybrid Cloud, DSPy, and Ollama for fully on-prem document processing.
- [Snapshots](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/edge/edge-api/snapshots/index.md): Reference for Qdrant Edge snapshot methods: unpacking a snapshot, reading the snapshot manifest, and applying a snapshot to an existing shard.
- [Working with ColBERT](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/fastembed/fastembed-colbert/index.md): Use FastEmbed to generate ColBERT multivectors and index them in Qdrant for late-interaction retrieval and reranking with native multivector support.
- [Movie Recommendation System](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/recommendation-system-ovhcloud/index.md): Build a collaborative-filtering movie recommender on OVHcloud with Qdrant Hybrid Cloud and sparse vectors for fast, private personalized recommendations.
- [Blog-Reading Chatbot with GPT-4o](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/rag-chatbot-scaleway/index.md): Deploy a RAG chatbot on Scaleway with Qdrant Hybrid Cloud, LangChain, and OpenAI, ingesting blog content for accurate, retrieval-augmented responses.
- [From Redis](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-redis/index.md): Migrate from Redis to Qdrant by streaming vectors and metadata out of RediSearch FT indexes and into Qdrant collections with the Qdrant Migration Tool.
- [From MongoDB](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-mongodb/index.md): Migrate from MongoDB to Qdrant by exporting documents and vector fields from MongoDB Atlas and loading them into Qdrant collections for dedicated vector search.
- [Reranking with FastEmbed](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/fastembed/fastembed-rerankers/index.md): Use cross-encoder rerankers with FastEmbed and Qdrant to re-score initial search results, trading speed for higher precision on a small candidate set.
- [From FAISS](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-faiss/index.md): Migrate from FAISS to Qdrant by importing non-quantized FAISS index files into Qdrant collections for managed storage, payload filters, and distributed search.
- [Multi-Vector Postprocessing](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/fastembed/fastembed-postprocessing/index.md): Use FastEmbed's MUVERA postprocessing to convert multivector embeddings into single-vector approximations, enabling fast HNSW retrieval with multivector reranking.
- [From Apache Solr](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-solr/index.md): Migrate from Apache Solr to Qdrant by streaming dense vector fields, document IDs, and metadata from Solr collections into Qdrant with the Qdrant Migration Tool.
- [From Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-qdrant/index.md): Replicate collections between Qdrant instances or within the same cluster, automatically recreating vector config, HNSW settings, quantization, and sharding.
- [Installation](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/installation/index.md): Install Qdrant via Docker, Kubernetes, or binary releases — review CPU, memory, storage, and networking requirements for self-hosted deployments.
- [Local Quickstart](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/quickstart/index.md): Quickstart guide to running Qdrant locally with Docker, connecting an SDK, and building a first collection for semantic vector search.
- [Capacity Planning](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/capacity-planning/index.md): Plan Qdrant cluster capacity: estimate RAM and disk for vectors, payloads, indexes, replication, and quantization to match your workload.
- [Cloud Quickstart](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud-quickstart/index.md): Create a free Qdrant Cloud cluster, install the client SDK, and run your first semantic search using built-in inference for vector embeddings.
- [Migration and Recovery](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migration-recovery-options/index.md): Decide between Qdrant's three data movement options — migration tool, collection snapshots, and cloud backups — based on use case, resource requirements, and operational trade-offs.
- [Snapshots](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/snapshots/index.md): Create, list, and restore Qdrant snapshots to back up collections, recover from failures, and replicate vector search deployments across clusters.
- [Upgrades](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/upgrades/index.md): Upgrade Qdrant clusters across Cloud, Kubernetes, Docker, and Compose with rolling restarts, version compatibility rules, and zero-downtime planning.
- [Security](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/security/index.md): Secure a Qdrant instance with Admin API keys, read-only API keys, JWT-based access control for collection-scoped permissions, network binding, and TLS encryption.
- [Production Checklist](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/production-checklist/index.md): Production-readiness checklist for Qdrant: distributed sharding, replication, quantization, load balancing, and monitoring for stable vector search.
- [Troubleshooting](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/common-errors/index.md): Troubleshoot common Qdrant runtime errors: open-file limits, HTTP 507 quota rejections, POSIX file system requirements, and recovery from corrupted collection metadata.
- [Static Embeddings](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-search-engineering/static-embeddings/index.md): Tutorial: apply static embedding models in Qdrant to deliver fast, low-resource semantic search with quality close to transformer-based embeddings.
- [Getting Started](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud-getting-started/index.md): Onboarding guide for Qdrant Managed Cloud — set up your account, size and create clusters, and prepare a production-ready vector search deployment.
- [Account Setup](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud-account-setup/index.md): Register a Qdrant Cloud account with email, Google, GitHub, or SSO. Create and switch between multiple Cloud accounts, manage account settings, and transfer ownership.
- [User Profile](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud-user-profile/index.md): Manage your personal Qdrant Cloud user profile — profile details, appearance and color scheme, cookie consent, pending account invitations and user deactivation.
- [Qdrant Web UI](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/web-ui/index.md): Use the Qdrant Web UI to manage collections, run REST API calls, upload snapshots, and explore vector data for local and Cloud deployments.
- [API & SDKs](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/interfaces/index.md): Connect to Qdrant with REST or gRPC APIs and official client libraries for Python, JavaScript, Rust, Go, Java, and .NET to build vector search apps.
- [Cloud Security](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud-security/index.md): Qdrant Cloud security: isolated clusters, encryption at rest and in transit, RBAC, API key controls, IP restrictions, and SOC 2 and HIPAA compliance.
- [Qdrant Cloud API](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud-api/index.md): Use the Qdrant Cloud API over gRPC or REST/JSON to automate clusters, backups, authentication, and Hybrid Cloud environments programmatically.
- [Qdrant Cloud CLI](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud-cli/index.md): Install and use the qcloud CLI to manage Qdrant Cloud clusters, API keys, and accounts directly from your terminal with scriptable commands.
- [Billing & Payments](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud-pricing-payments/index.md): Qdrant Cloud billing explained: usage-based pricing for CPU, memory, and disk, with payment via credit card or AWS, GCP, and Azure Marketplaces.
- [Premium Tier](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud-premium/index.md): Qdrant Cloud Premium adds 24/7 support, stronger uptime SLAs, SSO, VPC private links, multi-AZ topology, and customer-managed encryption keys.
- [Agent Skills](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/skills/index.md): Qdrant agent skills help AI coding assistants diagnose and tune vector search in production. Pass a skill URL from skills.qdrant.tech to your agent to get targeted guidance on scaling, search quality, performance, monitoring, and more.
- [Qdrant MCP Server](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/qdrant-mcp-server/index.md): Use the Qdrant MCP server to expose vector search as tools for AI assistants — power memory, retrieval, and context for agentic applications.
- [Support](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/support/index.md): Get help from Qdrant Cloud support — submit tickets through the support portal with the right request type, severity, and diagnostic information.
- [Overview](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-lp-overview/index.md): Tutorial hub for Qdrant — basics, search engineering, retrieval quality, operations and scale, migrations, and ecosystem integrations all in one place.
- [Practice Datasets](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/datasets/index.md): Download pre-computed Qdrant snapshots of public datasets like arXiv and Hugging Face collections to practice vector search without generating embeddings.
- [Agno](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/agno/index.md): Use Qdrant as the knowledge base for Agno multi-agent systems to give agents persistent memory and fast retrieval over documents and external data.
- [Airbyte](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/airbyte/index.md): Use Airbyte as a managed ELT pipeline into Qdrant, replicating records from databases, SaaS apps, and files into vector collections for semantic search.
- [Aleph Alpha](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/aleph-alpha/index.md): Use Aleph Alpha embeddings with Qdrant to power multilingual and multimodal semantic search, mapping text and images into a single vector space.
- [Apache Airflow](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/airflow/index.md): Orchestrate data loading into Qdrant with Apache Airflow, using the Qdrant provider to schedule, monitor, and recover vector ingestion DAGs in production.
- [Apache Spark](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/spark/index.md): Use the Qdrant-Spark connector to load embeddings and payloads from large Spark DataFrames into Qdrant collections for distributed vector ingestion at scale.
- [Apify](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/apify/index.md): Crawl websites with Apify and ingest the cleaned content into Qdrant collections to build RAG and semantic search applications on fresh web data.
- [AutoGen](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/autogen/index.md): Use Microsoft AutoGen with Qdrant to build multi-agent RAG workflows where cooperating LLM agents retrieve and reason over documents stored as vectors.
- [AWS Bedrock](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/bedrock/index.md): Combine AWS Bedrock embedding models with Qdrant for scalable semantic search and retrieval-augmented generation across your AWS-hosted data.
- [AWS Lakechain](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/lakechain/index.md): Deploy AWS document processing pipelines with Project Lakechain that write embeddings into Qdrant collections via the Qdrant storage connector and CDK.
- [BuildShip](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/buildship/index.md): Use the Qdrant integration in BuildShip to build low-code AI workflows, APIs, and scheduled jobs with semantic search over your vector collections.
- [CamelAI](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/camel/index.md): Integrate Qdrant with CAMEL-AI as the vector storage backend for agent memory and retrieval, powering LLM agents that solve real-world tasks with grounded data.
- [Cheshire Cat](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/cheshire-cat/index.md): Use Qdrant as the vector memory for Cheshire Cat agents, with built-in support for aliases, quantization, and snapshots for fast and durable retrieval.
- [Chonkie](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/chonkie/index.md): Use Chonkie to chunk and embed documents, then index them into Qdrant in a single SDK flow for retrieval-augmented generation and semantic search apps.
- [CocoIndex](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/cocoindex/index.md): Run real-time, incremental ETL with CocoIndex to transform raw data into embeddings and load them into Qdrant collections for AI retrieval workloads.
- [Cognee](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/cognee/index.md): Cognee ships a Qdrant adapter and documents Qdrant as a preferred, built-in vector database option. That means you configure one URI and key, and Cognee's pipelines will read/write embeddings directly to Qdrant while building and querying the graph.
- [Cohere](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/cohere/index.md): Use Cohere embedding models with Qdrant for semantic search, RAG, and classification, indexing documents and queries with task-specific input types.
- [Confluent Kafka](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/confluent/index.md): Connect Confluent Cloud Kafka to Qdrant with the managed sink connector, streaming records from topics into vector collections for real-time AI applications.
- [CrewAI](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/crewai/index.md): Use Qdrant as the memory store for CrewAI agents, powering short-term and entity memory with vector search for richer multi-agent collaboration.
- [Dagster](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/dagster/index.md): Use the Qdrant Dagster integration to build observable AI data pipelines that ingest documents, manage collections, and run vector search from Dagster assets.
- [Datadog](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/observability/datadog/index.md): Install the Datadog integration for Qdrant to collect real-time metrics on REST, gRPC, and cluster health and visualize them in your Datadog dashboards.
- [DeepEval](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/deepeval/index.md): Use DeepEval to test Qdrant-powered RAG pipelines, measuring answer relevancy, faithfulness, hallucination, and contextual precision over retrieved vector results.
- [Deploy Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/deploy-intro/index.md): Choose how to deploy Qdrant: Managed Cloud, Hybrid Cloud, Private Cloud, or self-hosted via Docker, Kubernetes, or bare-metal installation.
- [DLT](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/dlt/index.md): Use DLT as a Python data load tool to extract from arbitrary sources and write structured records and embeddings into Qdrant as a vector destination.
- [Dynamiq](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/dynamiq/index.md): Use Qdrant in Dynamiq Gen AI workflows for document writing, retrieval, and agent memory to power RAG pipelines and tool-augmented LLM agents.
- [Explore the Qdrant Ecosystem](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/ecosystem/index.md): Discover the Qdrant ecosystem — integrations with frameworks, embedding providers, cloud platforms, and community-built tools for vector search.
- [Feast](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/feast/index.md): Configure Qdrant as the online vector store in the Feast feature store to serve embedding features and similarity searches for production ML systems.
- [FiftyOne](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/fifty-one/index.md): Use Qdrant with FiftyOne to power image and text similarity search across computer vision datasets and improve dataset quality and model insights.
- [Firebase Genkit](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/genkit/index.md): Use the Qdrant Genkit plugin to add semantic retrieval and indexing to Firebase Genkit AI apps, with configurable embedders and collection options.
- [Fusion Embedding 2](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/fusion-embedding-2/index.md): Use EximiusLabs Fusion Embedding 2, an open-weight multimodal embedding model, with Qdrant to index and search content in a shared vector space. This guide covers the text path.
- [Gemini](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/gemini/index.md): Generate Google Gemini embeddings for text and multimodal content, then index them in Qdrant to build multilingual, cross-modal semantic search.
- [Google ADK](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/google-adk/index.md): Use Qdrant with Google ADK agents through the Qdrant MCP Server, giving agents semantic memory and retrieval tools for storing and recalling information.
- [Haystack](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/haystack/index.md): Use the Qdrant document store with Haystack to build generative AI, QA, and semantic search pipelines with full control over collection and quantization options.
- [HoneyHive](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/honeyhive/index.md): Use HoneyHive to trace and evaluate Qdrant vector search in RAG pipelines, monitoring latency, retrieval relevance, and embedding quality at scale.
- [InfinyOn Fluvio](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/fluvio/index.md): Use the Qdrant Fluvio connector to stream events from Fluvio topics into Qdrant collections, powering real-time vector search and event-driven AI workflows.
- [Jina Embeddings](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/jina-embeddings/index.md): Use Jina AI embeddings with Qdrant for multilingual semantic search, code retrieval, and long-context indexing with task-specific adapters and Matryoshka dimensions.
- [Keboola](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/keboola/index.md): Integrate Qdrant with Keboola to build data pipelines that generate embeddings, manage collections, and orchestrate vector search across your stack.
- [Kotaemon](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/kotaemon/index.md): Use Qdrant as the vector store in Kotaemon to power a customizable open-source RAG interface for ingesting and chatting with your own documents.
- [LangChain](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/langchain/index.md): Use the LangChain Qdrant integration to power semantic search and RAG with dense, sparse, and hybrid retrieval over your documents and embeddings.
- [LangChain4j](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/langchain4j/index.md): Integrate Qdrant with LangChain4j as the embedding store for Java AI apps, powering retrieval-augmented generation and semantic search over your data.
- [LangGraph](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/langgraph/index.md): Use Qdrant retrieval tools in LangGraph workflows to build stateful, multi-actor agents that combine LangChain components with hybrid vector search.
- [LlamaIndex](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/llama-index/index.md): Use Qdrant as the vector store in LlamaIndex to ingest private data and augment LLM apps with semantic retrieval and retrieval-augmented generation.
- [Make.com](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/make/index.md): Connect Qdrant to Make.com using the official app, automating vector search inside no-code scenarios that link Qdrant to thousands of other services.
- [Mastra](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/mastra/index.md): Use Qdrant with the Mastra TypeScript framework as the vector store for RAG, agents, and workflows running locally or in serverless cloud environments.
- [Mem0](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/mem0/index.md): Configure Mem0 to use Qdrant as its vector store backend, giving LLM applications a self-improving memory layer with personalized, long-term user recall.
- [Microsoft GraphRAG](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/microsoft-graphrag/index.md): Use Qdrant as a custom vector store backend for Microsoft GraphRAG to combine graph-based indexing with high-performance vector search for grounded LLM responses.
- [Microsoft NLWeb](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/nlweb/index.md): Use Microsoft NLWeb with Qdrant as the retrieval engine to build natural language interfaces for websites, powered by Schema.org, RSS, and the MCP protocol.
- [Mistral](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/mistral/index.md): Use Mistral Embed with Qdrant for semantic search and RAG, and apply binary quantization to shrink vector storage while preserving retrieval quality.
- [MixedBread](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/mixedbread/index.md): Generate MixedBread embeddings and store them in Qdrant to power smarter, faster semantic search across documents, code, and multi-domain knowledge bases.
- [Mixpeek](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/mixpeek/index.md): Pair Mixpeek video embeddings with Qdrant to chunk, index, and search video content using text or video queries for scalable multimodal retrieval.
- [N8N](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/n8n/index.md): Use the official Qdrant node in n8n to build automation workflows with semantic search, managing collections and points directly from your scenarios.
- [Neo4j GraphRAG](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/neo4j-graphrag/index.md): Use the Neo4j GraphRAG package with Qdrant as a vector retriever to combine graph-based knowledge with fast vector search for retrieval-augmented generation.
- [Nomic](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/nomic/index.md): Use open-source Nomic text embeddings with Qdrant via the Nomic SDK or FastEmbed to build long-context semantic search and retrieval pipelines.
- [Nvidia](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/nvidia/index.md): Pair NVIDIA embedding models with Qdrant to power semantic search and RAG, using NVIDIA's retrieval API for high-quality query and passage embeddings.
- [Ollama](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/ollama/index.md): Use Ollama to generate local embeddings and store them in Qdrant — power private, on-device retrieval-augmented generation without leaving your machine.
- [OpenAI](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/openai/index.md): Index OpenAI embeddings in Qdrant for semantic search and retrieval-augmented generation, and apply binary quantization to shrink storage with minimal quality loss.
- [Pipedream](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/pipedream/index.md): Integrate Qdrant with Pipedream to build automated cross-platform workflows that combine vector search with thousands of supported apps and APIs.
- [POMA](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/poma/index.md): Combine POMA's structure-preserving chunking with Qdrant to turn documents into chunksets and load them into vector collections for higher-quality retrieval.
- [Power Apps](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/powerapps/index.md): Connect Qdrant to Microsoft Power Apps with the official connector, adding vector search to custom business applications and Power Platform flows.
- [Prem AI](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/premai/index.md): Use PremAI's generative AI platform to create embeddings and index them in Qdrant for semantic search, RAG, and monitored, fine-tunable retrieval workflows.
- [PrivateGPT](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/privategpt/index.md): Use Qdrant as the default vector store in PrivateGPT to ingest and query your documents privately with local LLMs and full offline support.
- [Redpanda Connect](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/redpanda/index.md): Use Redpanda Connect to define YAML streaming pipelines that route records into Qdrant collections with at-least-once delivery for real-time vector ingestion.
- [Rig-rs](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/rig-rs/index.md): Use Rig with Qdrant in Rust to build modular LLM applications with semantic retrieval, ingesting documents and querying them through the Qdrant vector store.
- [RocketRide](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/rocketride/index.md): Use Qdrant in RocketRide to ingest embedded documents, retrieve context for RAG, and expose vector search, upsert, and delete operations to AI agents.
- [Salesforce Mulesoft](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/mulesoft/index.md): Integrate Qdrant with Salesforce MuleSoft Anypoint via the MuleSoft Vectors connector to add vector search and AI capabilities to enterprise integrations.
- [Semantic Search 101](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-basics/search-beginners-local/index.md): Tutorial: build a local semantic search engine with Qdrant in minutes by encoding text into embeddings and running vector queries with the Python client.
- [Semantic-Router](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/semantic-router/index.md): Use Semantic-Router with Qdrant as the vector index to make decision-layer routing for LLM agents based on semantic similarity rather than LLM generations.
- [SmolAgents](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/smolagents/index.md): Build Hugging Face SmolAgents that call Qdrant retrieval tools to query vector collections, combining code-driven agents with semantic search over your data.
- [Snowflake Models](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/snowflake/index.md): Use Snowflake Arctic Embed text models with Qdrant via FastEmbed to build efficient semantic search with compact, high-recall sentence embeddings.
- [Spring AI](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/spring-ai/index.md): Use Qdrant as the vector store in Spring AI to build Java AI apps with Spring-friendly abstractions for embeddings, semantic search, and RAG pipelines.
- [Stanford DSPy](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/dspy/index.md): Configure DSPy to use Qdrant as its retrieval model, grounding declarative LLM programs and RAG modules in fast vector search over your collections.
- [Superlinked](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/superlinked/index.md): Use Superlinked's self-hosted inference engine to generate dense, sparse, and multivector embeddings, and store them in Qdrant for hybrid vector search.
- [Swiftide](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/swiftide/index.md): Use Swiftide with Qdrant in Rust to build streaming indexing and querying pipelines for LLM apps, supporting dense and hybrid sparse/dense vector search.
- [Sycamore](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/sycamore/index.md): Use the Sycamore Qdrant connector to write and read embeddings for PDFs, HTML, and other unstructured documents, powering GenAI, RAG, and document analytics.
- [Testcontainers](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/testcontainers/index.md): Use Testcontainers to launch disposable Qdrant instances for end-to-end integration tests across Java, Go, Node.js, Python, and .NET projects.
- [ToolJet](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/tooljet/index.md): Use the Qdrant plugin in ToolJet to build low-code business apps with vector search, managing collections, points, and filtered queries through drag-and-drop.
- [Twelve Labs](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/twelvelabs/index.md): Use Twelve Labs Embed API with Qdrant to index video, text, image, and audio in one vector space and run any-to-any cross-modal similarity search.
- [txtai](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/txtai/index.md): Configure txtai to use Qdrant as its embedding backend, building semantic search apps over Transformer-based neural embeddings with high-performance vector search.
- [Unstructured](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/unstructured/index.md): Use Unstructured to parse PDFs, HTML, and office files, then ingest the cleaned text and embeddings into Qdrant collections for RAG and semantic search.
- [Upstage](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/upstage/index.md): Use Upstage Solar Embeddings with Qdrant to build fast text retrieval and RAG, leveraging dual query and passage models in a unified vector space.
- [Vanna.AI](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/vanna-ai/index.md): Use Qdrant as the vector store for Vanna.AI text-to-SQL agents, training RAG models on schema and documentation to generate accurate SQL for your database.
- [VectaX - Mirror Security](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/mirror-security/index.md): Combine Mirror Security VectaX with Qdrant to encrypt vector embeddings and enforce role-based access control on semantic search and retrieval.
- [Vectorize.io](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/vectorize/index.md): Integrate Vectorize.io with Qdrant to deploy real-time RAG pipelines, automatically extracting data, generating embeddings, and keeping collections fresh.
- [VoltAgent](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/voltagent/index.md): Use VoltAgent with Qdrant retrievers to build observable TypeScript AI agents, combining modular tool integration with semantic search over your knowledge base.
- [Voyage AI](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/voyage/index.md): Use Voyage AI embeddings with Qdrant to run high-quality semantic search and RAG, generating dense vectors for documents and queries via the Voyage API.
- [Welcome to Qdrant Cloud](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud-intro/index.md): Overview of Qdrant Cloud: managed vector search infrastructure spanning Managed Cloud, Hybrid Cloud, and Private Cloud deployment options.

## Qdrant Academy
- [How ColPali Models Work](https://qdrant.tech/course/multi-vector-search/module-2/how-colpali-works/index.md): Understand the inner workings of ColPali models and how they generate multi-vector representations for images and documents.
- [Late Interaction Basics](https://qdrant.tech/course/multi-vector-search/module-1/late-interaction-basics/index.md): Understand the late interaction paradigm and how it differs from traditional dense embeddings for text search.
- [Module Overview](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-0/module-overview/index.md): Set up Qdrant and build your first vector search app. Learn how to configure Qdrant Cloud, run a basic search, and get started with the fundamentals.
- [Module Overview](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-1/module-overview/index.md): Understand why traditional search struggles and how modern semantic search improves it. Learn about embeddings, distance metrics, and hybrid search systems.
- [Module Overview](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-2/module-overview/index.md): Understand collections, points, vectors, payloads, HNSW, chunking, and the ingestion pipeline. Move from theory to actual system design in Qdrant.
- [Module Overview](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-3/module-overview/index.md): Compare dense and sparse retrieval, see where each one fails on real queries, and build a hybrid search pipeline in Qdrant with rank fusion and filters.
- [Module Overview](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-4/module-overview/index.md): Design a vector search system in Qdrant: what to decide before ingesting, what changes as data grows, where generation fits, and where to run it.
- [Module Overview](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-5/module-overview/index.md): Build the Beginners capstone: ingest news, transcripts, and satellite imagery on shared points, cluster them into risk themes, and query every modality.
- [Module Overview](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-6/module-overview/index.md): Match a search problem to the Qdrant feature that fixes it: score boosting, MMR diversity, reranking, grouping, relevance feedback, and discovery.
- [Multi-Stage Retrieval with Universal Query API](https://qdrant.tech/course/multi-vector-search/module-3/multi-stage-retrieval/index.md): Combine multiple optimization techniques in multi-stage retrieval pipelines using Qdrant's Universal Query API.
- [Qdrant Setup](https://qdrant.tech/course/multi-vector-search/module-0/qdrant-setup/index.md): Set up Qdrant for multi-vector search. Learn how to create a collection and configure it for multi-vector embeddings.
- [ColPali Family Overview](https://qdrant.tech/course/multi-vector-search/module-2/colpali-family/index.md): Explore the ColPali model family and their capabilities for multi-modal document understanding and retrieval.
- [Final Project: Production-Ready Documentation Search Engine](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-6/final-project/index.md): Create a complete documentation search system with Qdrant, featuring hybrid retrieval, multivector reranking, and performance evaluation for a portfolio-ready, production-quality vector search application.
- [Find Your Problem](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-6/find-your-problem/index.md): Pair each common search problem with the feature that addresses it, and see which stage of a query that feature runs in.
- [From Idea to System](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-2/from-idea-to-system/index.md): Move from theory to system design. See every building block that takes raw text to a running Qdrant collection, and how they fit together.
- [HNSW Indexing Fundamentals](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-2/what-is-hnsw/index.md): Learn how HNSW indexing powers fast, scalable vector search in Qdrant. Understand parameters like m, ef_construct, and hnsw_ef to balance recall, speed, and memory efficiency.
- [Installing Dependencies](https://qdrant.tech/course/multi-vector-search/module-0/installing-dependencies/index.md): Install Python dependencies including FastEmbed and Qdrant client.
- [Integrating with Haystack](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-7/haystack/index.md): Learn how Qdrant and Haystack combine to deliver end-to-end search and recommendation systems with hybrid retrieval, semantic filtering, and agentic AI orchestration.
- [MaxSim Distance Metric](https://qdrant.tech/course/multi-vector-search/module-1/maxsim-distance/index.md): Learn about the MaxSim distance metric used in multi-vector search and how it computes similarity between multi-vector representations.
- [Multivectors for Late Interaction Models](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-5/colbert-multivectors/index.md): Learn how Qdrant supports late interaction models like ColBERT and ColPali using multivectors for token-level precision, enabling fine-grained, context-aware text and visual document retrieval.
- [Points, Vectors and Payloads](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-1/embedding-models/index.md): Learn Qdrant’s core data model with points, vectors, payloads, and named vectors. Compare dense, sparse, and multivectors, understand dimensionality trade-offs, and master filtering with payload indexes for precise retrieval.
- [Project Overview](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-5/project-overview/index.md): One factory fire reaches an analyst four ways. Build the system that connects a news report, a satellite image, an earnings call, and a filing.
- [Qdrant Setup](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-0/qdrant-cloud/index.md): Set up your Qdrant Cloud cluster in minutes. Learn to create collections, manage data, access the Web UI, and connect securely from Python.
- [Sparse Vectors and Inverted Indexes](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-3/sparse-vectors/index.md): Learn sparse vectors and inverted indexes in Qdrant, create named sparse vectors, store index–value pairs, run exact dot-product search, and prepare for hybrid search with dense vectors.
- [Vector Quantization Methods](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-4/what-is-quantization/index.md): Explore scalar, binary, and product quantization in Qdrant. Learn how compression boosts vector search speed, cuts memory costs, and balances accuracy for large-scale AI retrieval.
- [Vector Quantization Techniques](https://qdrant.tech/course/multi-vector-search/module-3/quantization-techniques/index.md): Learn how to reduce memory usage with scalar quantization, binary quantization, and other compression methods.
- [What Is Search?](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-1/what-is-search/index.md): Understand what search really does: match a question against a collection, then rank what comes back. The foundation for every retrieval system in this course.
- [Where Design Decisions Live](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-4/where-design-decisions-live/index.md): A vector search system has five layers, ordered from easiest to hardest to change. Learn which decisions you can revise and which force a rebuild.
- [Where We Left Off](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-3/where-we-left-off/index.md): Dense retrieval handles meaning well and gets shaky on the part of a query that has to be exact. See where Module 2's pipeline falls short.
- [Accuracy Recovery with Rescoring](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-4/rescoring-oversampling-indexing/index.md): Learn how oversampling and rescoring restore accuracy in quantized vector search. Improve Qdrant search precision while maintaining high performance using efficient reranking on original vectors.
- [Combining Vector Search and Filtering](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-2/filterable-hnsw/index.md): Learn how Qdrant combines HNSW vector search with payload filtering. Understand Filterable HNSW, query planning, and payload indexing for accurate, high-performance retrieval.
- [Core Data Model](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-2/core-data-model/index.md): Learn how Qdrant organizes data in three levels: collections hold points, points hold vectors and payloads. The foundation for everything that follows.
- [Course Completion and Next Steps](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-6/congratulations/index.md): Complete your Qdrant course by earning certification and mastering hybrid, multivector, and production-ready vector search techniques—skills to design, evaluate, and deploy real-world AI search systems.
- [Decide Before You Ingest](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-4/decide-before-you-ingest/index.md): Four decisions belong to the data layer: what you embed, the model, the chunk size, and the payload schema. Changing any one means ingesting again.
- [Demo: Keyword Search with Sparse Vectors](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-3/sparse-retrieval-demo/index.md): Hands-on sparse retrieval in Qdrant—create BM25 collections, enable IDF, index with FastEmbed, try SPLADE++ expansion, and execute keyword queries via the Universal Query API.
- [Distance Metrics](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-1/distance-metrics/index.md): Learn how distance metrics like cosine, Euclidean, Manhattan, and dot product shape vector similarity in Qdrant. Discover which metric fits your data and use case.
- [Implementing a Basic Vector Search](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-0/building-simple-vector-search/index.md): Learn how to build a basic vector search in Qdrant. Create collections, insert vectors, and run your first similarity search step-by-step with Python.
- [Integrating with Unstructured.io](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-7/unstructured/index.md): Learn how Unstructured.io and Qdrant transform unstructured enterprise data into structured embeddings through VLM document understanding, smart chunking, and secure, production-ready ETL pipelines.
- [Measure First](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-6/measure-first/index.md): Ranking changes are hard to judge by eye. Build a golden set, then pick between Recall@K, Mean Reciprocal Rank, and Normalized Discounted Cumulative Gain.
- [Pooling Techniques](https://qdrant.tech/course/multi-vector-search/module-3/pooling-techniques/index.md): Reduce the number of vectors per document using row/column pooling and hierarchical token pooling strategies.
- [Qdrant Setup](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-0/qdrant-cloud/index.md): Set up your Qdrant Cloud cluster in minutes. Learn to create collections, manage data, access the Web UI, and connect securely from Python.
- [System Architecture](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-5/system-architecture/index.md): The capstone has four stages: ingest, embed, store, then cluster and query. See how each maps to Qdrant primitives you already know.
- [The Two Families of Search](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-3/the-two-families-of-search/index.md): Compare the two families every retrieval system is built from: dense vectors that find what a query means, and sparse vectors that find what it says.
- [The Universal Query API](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-5/universal-query-api/index.md): Learn how to run dense, sparse, and ColBERT multivector retrieval with Qdrant’s Universal Query API—fusing, filtering, and reranking results in a single atomic request.
- [Use Cases for Multi-Vector Search](https://qdrant.tech/course/multi-vector-search/module-1/use-cases-multi-vector/index.md): Discover scenarios where multi-vector search outperforms single-vector embeddings and provides better retrieval quality.
- [Visual Interpretability of ColPali](https://qdrant.tech/course/multi-vector-search/module-2/visual-interpretability/index.md): Learn how to visualize and interpret ColPali embeddings to understand what the model focuses on in images.
- [Why Keyword Search Struggles](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-1/why-keyword-search-struggles/index.md): See why keyword search misses relevant results when people phrase the same intent differently, and where exact word matching runs out of road.
- [Demo: HNSW Performance Tuning](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-2/collection-tuning-demo/index.md): Tune Qdrant’s HNSW index for speed and precision. Optimize bulk uploads, test filters, and benchmark performance on a real 100K OpenAI embedding dataset.
- [Demo: Universal Query for Hybrid Retrieval](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-5/universal-query-demo/index.md): Build a hybrid research discovery system using Qdrant’s Universal Query API—combine dense, sparse, and ColBERT vectors for semantic, keyword, and reranked retrieval in one query.
- [Distance Metrics](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-2/distance-metrics/index.md): Choose a distance metric when you create a collection. Learn why cosine similarity fits most text embeddings, and how to match the metric to your model.
- [How Traditional Search Improved](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-1/how-traditional-search-improved/index.md): Traditional search gained stemming, typo tolerance, and relevance ranking, but it still matches words. Learn what semantic search adds on top.
- [Hybrid Search and the Universal Query API](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-3/hybrid-search/index.md): Master hybrid search in Qdrant using dense and sparse vectors. Explore retrieval, reranking, and Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF) to build efficient, adaptive search experiences.
- [Hybrid Search: Dense and Sparse](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-3/hybrid-search/index.md): Hybrid search runs dense and sparse retrieval in the same request and merges their ranked lists into one result set. Learn how fusion works.
- [Implementing a Basic Vector Search](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-0/building-simple-vector-search/index.md): Learn how to build a basic vector search in Qdrant. Create collections, insert vectors, and run your first similarity search step-by-step with Python.
- [Integrating with Tensorlake](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-7/tensorlake/index.md): Learn how TensorLake and Qdrant combine document parsing, knowledge graphs, and vector search to build scalable, structured data lakes for advanced RAG and research discovery applications.
- [Large-Scale Data Ingestion](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-4/large-scale-ingestion/index.md): Master large-scale vector ingestion in Qdrant. Compare upsert, upload_points, and upload_collection, and learn how to stream a large dataset into a collection without loading it into memory.
- [MUVERA](https://qdrant.tech/course/multi-vector-search/module-3/muvera/index.md): Understand MUVERA and how it enables HNSW indexing for multi-vector search despite MaxSim asymmetry.
- [Problems of Multi-Vector Search](https://qdrant.tech/course/multi-vector-search/module-1/problems-multi-vector/index.md): Understand the challenges and limitations of multi-vector search at scale, including memory and performance considerations.
- [Project: Building Your First Vector Search System](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-0/pitstop-project/index.md): Apply your Qdrant skills to build a complete vector search system. Create collections, insert data, run similarity and filtered searches, and share your results.
- [Ranking: Score Boosting and Reranking](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-6/ranking-and-reranking/index.md): Two ways to change result order: rescore candidates with a formula query and decay functions, or reorder a shortlist with a cross-encoder reranker.
- [Signal Sources and Embedding Models](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-5/signal-sources-and-embedding-models/index.md): Two models cover every signal in the capstone. Learn why the collection declares three named vectors rather than five, and what CLIP puts in one space.
- [Text Chunking Strategies](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-1/chunking-strategies/index.md): Learn how to split text into meaningful chunks for vector search. Compare six chunking strategies and discover how metadata improves retrieval precision in Qdrant.
- [What Changes as the Collection Grows](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-4/what-changes-as-the-collection-grows/index.md): A three-article collection needs no tuning. At millions of points, the indexing and storage layers both need attention. Learn what changes and when.
- [Demo: Implementing a Hybrid Search System](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-3/hybrid-search-demo/index.md): Step-by-step demo on implementing hybrid search using Qdrant’s Universal Query API. Explore dense vs. sparse search, score fusion algorithms, and real-world evaluation techniques.
- [Demo: Semantic Movie Search](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-1/movie-search-system/index.md): Build a semantic movie search with Qdrant. Compare chunking strategies, embed descriptions, and combine cosine similarity with metadata filters and grouping for accurate, theme-aware recommendations.
- [Diversity: Maximal Marginal Relevance](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-6/diversity-mmr/index.md): Maximal Marginal Relevance picks results that match the query and differ from each other. Learn the candidates_limit trap that makes it look inert.
- [Evaluating Search Pipelines](https://qdrant.tech/course/multi-vector-search/module-3/evaluating-pipelines/index.md): Learn how to evaluate different search configurations in terms of cost, latency, and retrieval quality using ground truth datasets and standardized metrics.
- [Growing Past One Machine](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-4/growing-past-one-machine/index.md): Sharding splits a collection across nodes and replication survives losing one. Learn when each is worth adding, and why tuning usually comes first.
- [How It Works: Embeddings](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-1/embeddings/index.md): Learn how embedding models turn text into vectors that capture meaning, and generate your first embeddings locally with FastEmbed and Python.
- [Ingestion Pipeline](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-5/ingestion-pipeline/index.md): Build the daily job: collect signals, embed each modality, assign a risk score, and create every payload index analysts will filter on before ingesting.
- [Integrating with Superlinked](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-7/superlinked/index.md): Learn how Superlinked’s Mixture of Encoders and Qdrant enable rich, multi-modal embeddings that fuse semantic, numerical, and temporal data for optimized vector retrieval.
- [Multi-Vector Embeddings in Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/course/multi-vector-search/module-1/multi-vector-in-qdrant/index.md): Configure Qdrant collections for multi-vector embeddings and learn how to index and query multi-vector data.
- [Project: Building a Recommendation System](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-5/pitstop-project/index.md): Build a hybrid AI recommendation system with Qdrant’s Universal Query API—combining dense, sparse, and multivector retrieval, ColBERT reranking, and RRF fusion in one atomic query.
- [Project: HNSW Performance Benchmarking](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-2/pitstop-project/index.md): Optimize vector search with Qdrant. Test multiple HNSW configurations, time uploads and queries, and evaluate filtering with and without payload indexes to find the best settings for your domain.
- [Project: Quantization Performance Optimization](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-4/pitstop-project/index.md): Apply vector quantization in Qdrant to boost search speed, reduce memory, and balance accuracy. Test scalar, binary, and 2-bit quantization with oversampling and rescoring optimization.
- [Setting Up Hybrid Search in Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-3/hybrid-search-in-qdrant/index.md): Build hybrid search in Qdrant: store dense and sparse vectors on the same point, then use prefetch and the Query API to run and fuse both retrievers.
- [Top-K Retrieval](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-2/top-k-retrieval/index.md): See how Qdrant turns a query into a vector and returns the K most similar points, ranked by similarity score.
- [Clustering Risk Signals](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-5/clustering-risk-signals/index.md): Cluster signals that describe the same underlying event even when they arrive from different sources, using the shared text vector on every point.
- [Comparing Meaning: Distance Metrics](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-1/distance-metrics/index.md): Measure meaning with cosine similarity. Score related and unrelated phrases with NumPy, and see how context changes the similarity between two texts.
- [Fast Approximate Search: HNSW](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-2/hnsw/index.md): Learn how the HNSW graph index makes search over millions of vectors fast, and what recall you trade for that speed.
- [From Results to an Answer](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-4/from-results-to-an-answer/index.md): Retrieval-Augmented Generation sends a ranked list to a language model that writes an answer. See where generation sits relative to the search system.
- [Fusion Strategies](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-3/fusion-strategies/index.md): Compare the two fusion strategies. Reciprocal Rank Fusion uses position alone, while Distribution-Based Score Fusion rescales scores onto a comparable range.
- [Grouping: One Slot per Document](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-6/grouping/index.md): Group results by a payload field so one document takes one slot, and see why deduplicating after the search leaves the page short.
- [Integrating with LlamaIndex](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-7/llamaindex/index.md): Learn how LlamaIndex and Qdrant power intelligent RAG pipelines, function-calling agents, and cloud-synced vector search systems with structured workflows and dynamic query handling.
- [Project: Building a Hybrid Search Engine](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-3/pitstop-project/index.md): Build a hybrid search engine in Qdrant combining dense and sparse vectors with Reciprocal Rank Fusion. Compare performance, optimize retrieval, and understand when hybrid search outperforms single-vector methods.
- [Project: Building a Semantic Search Engine](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-1/pitstop-project/index.md): Build a semantic search engine with Qdrant. Compare chunking strategies, index embeddings, and query by meaning to discover what works best for your domain.
- [Analyst Queries](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-5/analyst-queries/index.md): Query the capstone collection the way an analyst would: across three named vectors, with filters, plus the centroid query from the clustering step.
- [Filtering: Works with Any Retrieval Method](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-3/filtering/index.md): Payload filters are not a hybrid-only feature. Apply the same conditions to dense, sparse, and hybrid retrieval, evaluated during the search.
- [Final Project: Build Your Own Multi-Vector Search System](https://qdrant.tech/course/multi-vector-search/module-3/final-project/index.md): Apply everything you've learned to build a multi-vector search system that solves a real problem of your choosing.
- [Payload Filtering](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-2/payload-filtering/index.md): Apply payload filters during HNSW traversal rather than after retrieval, so results stay both semantically relevant and logically valid.
- [Searching From Examples and Feedback](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-6/search-from-examples/index.md): Search from positive and negative examples with the Recommendation and Discovery APIs, and fold click feedback into the next query.
- [Where It Runs](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-4/where-it-runs/index.md): Deployment mode is independent of your design decisions. Compare the modes that run Qdrant as a server, and choose by ownership and isolation.
- [Why Similarity Alone Is Not Enough](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-1/why-similarity-is-not-enough/index.md): See where similarity breaks: negation, word order, and exact product codes. Learn why a payload filter, not a better model, is the fix.
- [Chunking Strategies](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-2/chunking-strategies/index.md): Every embedding model has a token limit, and text past it is dropped silently. Compare fixed-size, semantic, and sliding-window chunking.
- [Design Your Own System](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-4/design-your-own-system/index.md): Apply five questions to a system of your own, and turn what you know about layers, ingestion, and scale into a concrete design.
- [Inspecting a Collection](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-6/inspecting-a-collection/index.md): Two features for checking what you actually ingested: facet counts for how selective a filter would be, and random sampling for spot checks.
- [Integrating with Camel AI](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-7/camel/index.md): Learn how Camel AI and Qdrant enable automated RAG pipelines with multi-agent communication, vector-based memory, and seamless integration into live environments like Discord bots.
- [Knowledge Check](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-3/knowledge-check/index.md): Work through retrieval failures and decide what to add and why, before you move on to designing a full system.
- [Knowledge Check](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-5/knowledge-check/index.md): Work through these questions on named vectors, payload indexes, and clustering before you call the capstone project complete.
- [When a System Needs Both](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-1/when-a-system-needs-both/index.md): Learn when a search system needs both semantic matching and exact matching, and how the two approaches cover each other's blind spots.
- [Course Summary](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-5/course-summary/index.md): A recap of the Qdrant Beginner Course, from why keyword search struggles through to a multimodal capstone running on one collection.
- [Further Reading](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-1/further-reading/index.md): References for Module 1: distance metrics, how embedding models work, and the FastEmbed library used throughout this module.
- [Ingestion Pipeline: End-to-End](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-2/ingestion-pipeline/index.md): Put it together: connect to a cluster, create a collection and payload index, embed and upload points, then run your first filtered query.
- [Integrating with Jina AI](https://qdrant.tech/course/essentials/day-7/jina/index.md): Learn how Jina AI’s Embeddings v4 and Qdrant enable advanced multimodal retrieval, supporting text-to-image, image-to-text, and hybrid search with high-performance vector storage.
- [Knowledge Check](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-6/knowledge-check/index.md): Work through the traps in this module: an MMR recall drop, a decay term that decides every ranking, and a grouping request that returns a 400.
- [References and Further Reading](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-3/references-and-further-reading/index.md): References for Module 3: prefetch semantics, both fusion strategies and their tuning parameters, and filtering during search.
- [References and Further Reading](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-4/references-and-further-reading/index.md): References for Module 4: the sizing tool, distributed deployment mechanics, and further reading on tuning a collection as it grows.
- [Further Reading](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-2/further-reading/index.md): References for Module 2: a closer look at distance metrics, how the HNSW index is built and tuned, and the full chunking comparison.
- [References and Further Reading](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/module-5/references-and-further-reading/index.md): References for Module 5: named vectors, multimodal and multilingual search, and the APIs behind the capstone project.
- [Qdrant Multi-Vector Certification](https://qdrant.tech/course/multi-vector-search/certification/index.md): Get officially certified in multi-vector search by Qdrant.
- [Qdrant Beginner Certification](https://qdrant.tech/course/beginners/certification/index.md): Earn the official Qdrant Beginner certification: prove you can build collections, choose distance metrics, filter payloads, and run hybrid search.

