## Qdrant Articles
- [Hybrid Search in Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/articles/hybrid-search/index.md): Decide whether to add hybrid search in Qdrant: the queries dense and sparse retrieval each get wrong, and how to measure the gain.
- [What to Check Before Tuning a Qdrant Collection](https://qdrant.tech/articles/before-tuning-a-qdrant-collection/index.md): Audit a Qdrant collection: find the settings that degrade retrieval silently, choose the cheapest next change, and size a labeled query set.
- [Candidate Depth: How Much Retrieval Is Enough?](https://qdrant.tech/articles/candidate-depth/index.md): Set candidate depth and hnsw_ef in Qdrant, measure the gap between your ranking and a perfect one, and balance the trade-offs.
- [Qdrant Summer of Code 2024 - ONNX Cross Encoders in Python](https://qdrant.tech/articles/cross-encoder-integration-gsoc/index.md): A summary of my work and experience at Qdrant Summer of Code 2024.
- [How to Tune Hybrid Search in Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/articles/how-to-tune-hybrid-search/index.md): Tune hybrid search fusion in Qdrant: choose between RRF and DBSF, set the constant k from your relevance labels, and get weights right.
- [When Is a Reranker Worth It?](https://qdrant.tech/articles/when-a-reranker-is-worth-it/index.md): Test whether a cross-encoder reranker beats your tuned first stage in Qdrant, then choose the model and candidate count from measured results.
- [When Your Collection Outgrows RAM](https://qdrant.tech/articles/when-your-collection-outgrows-ram/index.md): Set quantization and memory placement in Qdrant once a collection outgrows RAM: what the rescoring disk read costs and what quality it recovers.
- [Predicting Weak Retrieval Without an LLM](https://qdrant.tech/articles/predicting-weak-retrieval/index.md): Detect weak retrieval with cheap signals from the result, no extra model call. Which one predicts failure depends on your corpus, so test it on your data.
- [Qdrant 1.8.0: Enhanced Search Capabilities for Better Results](https://qdrant.tech/articles/qdrant-1.8.x/index.md): Explore the latest in search technology with Qdrant 1.8.0! Discover faster performance, smarter indexing, and enhanced search capabilities.
- [Qdrant 1.7.0 has just landed!](https://qdrant.tech/articles/qdrant-1.7.x/index.md): Sparse vectors, Discovery API, user-defined sharding, and snapshot-based shard transfer. That's what you can find in the latest Qdrant 1.7.0 release!
- [Deliver Better Recommendations with Qdrant’s new API](https://qdrant.tech/articles/new-recommendation-api/index.md): Qdrant 1.6 brings recommendations strategies and more flexibility to the Recommendation API.
- [Google Summer of Code 2023 - Polygon Geo Filter for Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/articles/geo-polygon-filter-gsoc/index.md): A Summary of my work and experience at Qdrant's Gsoc '23.
- [Google Summer of Code 2023 - Web UI for Visualization and Exploration](https://qdrant.tech/articles/web-ui-gsoc/index.md): My journey as a Google Summer of Code 2023 student working on the "Web UI for Visualization and Exploration" project for Qdrant.
- [Qdrant Summer of Code 2024 - WASM based Dimension Reduction](https://qdrant.tech/articles/dimension-reduction-qsoc/index.md): My journey as a Qdrant Summer of Code 2024 participant working on enhancing vector visualization using WebAssembly (WASM) based dimension reduction.
- [Introducing Qdrant 1.3.0](https://qdrant.tech/articles/qdrant-1.3.x/index.md): New version is out! Our latest release brings about some exciting performance improvements and much-needed fixes.
- [Filtered Vector Search: What ACORN Fixes, and What Fixes ACORN](https://qdrant.tech/articles/filtered-vector-search-acorn/index.md): Benchmark filtered vector search in Qdrant: how ACORN, filterable HNSW, and query planning trade recall for latency on one million points.
- [On Unstructured Data, Vector Databases, New AI Age, and Our Seed Round.](https://qdrant.tech/articles/seed-round/index.md): We announce Qdrant seed round investment and share our thoughts on Vector Databases and New AI Age.
- [Memory Tiers in Qdrant: What to Use and When](https://qdrant.tech/articles/memory-tiers-in-qdrant-what-to-use-and-when/index.md): Which Qdrant memory tier layout to use and when, and why, backed by benchmarks.
- [Configure Qdrant's Optimizer for Predictable Search Latency](https://qdrant.tech/articles/tuning-qdrant-optimizer/index.md): Configuration guidance for Qdrant's indexing, merge, and vacuum optimizers, backed by search latency measurements across 13 configurations on a 1.76 million point collection.
- [Introducing Qdrant 1.2.x](https://qdrant.tech/articles/qdrant-1.2.x/index.md): Check out what Qdrant 1.2 brings to vector search
- [FastEmbed: Qdrant's Efficient Python Library for Embedding Generation](https://qdrant.tech/articles/fastembed/index.md): Learn how to accurately and efficiently create text embeddings with FastEmbed.
- [TurboQuant in Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/articles/turboquant-quantization/index.md): TurboQuant — a new rotation-based vector quantization algorithm from Google Research — now ships in Qdrant 1.18, with extensions that make it work on real embeddings.
- [Fine-Tuning Sparse Embeddings for E-Commerce Search | Part 1: Why Sparse Embeddings Beat BM25](https://qdrant.tech/articles/sparse-embeddings-ecommerce-part-1/index.md): Part 1 of a 5-part series on fine-tuning SPLADE sparse embeddings for e-commerce search. Learn how sparse embeddings outperform BM25 and dense models for product search, how SPLADE works, and why Qdrant's native sparse vector support matters.
- [Relevance Feedback in Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/articles/relevance-feedback/index.md): The story behind the vector search-native relevance feedback feature, available since 1.17.0, which increases the relevance of search results universally, cheaply, and at scale.
- [Building Performant, Scaled Agentic Vector Search with Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/articles/agentic-builders-guide/index.md): Learn how to build performant, scalable AI agents with efficient vector retrieval, hybrid dense-sparse search, real-time memory, multimodal context integration, and optimized architectures for low-latency, high-accuracy execution in production environments.
- [How to Choose an Embedding Model: Evaluation & Tradeoffs](https://qdrant.tech/articles/how-to-choose-an-embedding-model/index.md): Building proper search requires selecting the right embedding model for your specific use case. This guide helps you navigate the selection process based on performance, cost, and other practical considerations.
- [miniCOIL: on the Road to Usable Sparse Neural Retrieval](https://qdrant.tech/articles/minicoil/index.md): Introducing miniCOIL, a lightweight sparse neural retriever capable of generalization.
- [Data Exploration with Qdrant's Distance Matrix API](https://qdrant.tech/articles/distance-based-exploration/index.md): Explore your data under a new angle with Qdrant's tools for dimensionality reduction, clusterization, and visualization.
- [Introducing Gridstore: Qdrant's Custom Key-Value Store](https://qdrant.tech/articles/gridstore-key-value-storage/index.md): Why and how we built our own key-value store. A short technical report on our procedure and results.
- [Why Rust?](https://qdrant.tech/articles/why-rust/index.md): Qdrant could be built in any language. But it's written in Rust. Here*s why.
- [Fine-Tuning Sparse Embeddings for E-Commerce Search | Part 2: Training SPLADE on Modal](https://qdrant.tech/articles/sparse-embeddings-ecommerce-part-2/index.md): Part 2 of a 5-part series on fine-tuning SPLADE sparse embeddings for e-commerce search. Build a training pipeline on Modal with persistent checkpoints, SpladeLoss, and hyperparameter sweeps.
- [Vector Search in Production: Scaling, HA & Tuning Guide](https://qdrant.tech/articles/vector-search-production/index.md): We gathered our most recommended tips and tricks to make your production deployment run smoothly.
- [Relevance Feedback in Informational Retrieval](https://qdrant.tech/articles/search-feedback-loop/index.md): Relerance feedback: from ancient history to LLMs. Why relevance feedback techniques are good on paper but not popular in neural search, and what we can do about it.
- [Why Vector Search Needs a Dedicated Database](https://qdrant.tech/articles/dedicated-vector-search/index.md): Why add-on vector search looks good — until you actually use it.
- [What is Agentic RAG? Building Agents with Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/articles/agentic-rag/index.md): Agents are a new paradigm in AI, and they are changing how we build RAG systems. Learn how to build agents with Qdrant and which framework to choose.
- [Modern Sparse Neural Retrieval: From Theory to Practice](https://qdrant.tech/articles/modern-sparse-neural-retrieval/index.md): A comprehensive guide to modern sparse neural retrievers: COIL, TILDEv2, SPLADE, and more. Find out how they work and learn how to use them effectively.
- [Immutable Data Structures in Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/articles/immutable-data-structures/index.md): Learn how immutable data structures improve vector search performance in Qdrant.
- [Discovery Search in Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/articles/discovery-search/index.md): Discovery Search, an innovative way to constrain the vector space in which a search is performed, relying only on vectors.
- [Semantic Search As You Type](https://qdrant.tech/articles/search-as-you-type/index.md): To show off Qdrant's performance, we show how to do a quick search-as-you-type that will come back within a few milliseconds.
- [Fine-Tuning Sparse Embeddings for E-Commerce Search | Part 3: Evaluation and Hard Negatives](https://qdrant.tech/articles/sparse-embeddings-ecommerce-part-3/index.md): Part 3 of a 5-part series on fine-tuning SPLADE sparse embeddings for e-commerce search. Index products in Qdrant, run retrieval benchmarks, and implement ANCE-inspired hard negative mining for a 28% improvement over BM25.
- [What is a Vector Database?](https://qdrant.tech/articles/what-is-a-vector-database/index.md): Discover how vector databases power semantic search by understanding the meaning behind your data. This guide breaks down how they work and why they've become the backbone of modern AI search.
- [Late Interaction Retrieval with Dense Token Embeddings](https://qdrant.tech/articles/late-interaction-models/index.md): We recently discovered that embedding models can become late interaction models & can perform surprisingly well in some scenarios. See what we learned here.
- [Semantic Caching for RAG: Cut LLM Cost and Latency](https://qdrant.tech/articles/semantic-cache-ai-data-retrieval/index.md): Semantic cache is reshaping AI applications by enabling rapid data retrieval. Discover how its implementation benefits your RAG setup.
- [Multimodal Food Search Demo](https://qdrant.tech/articles/food-discovery-demo/index.md): Feeling hungry? Find the perfect meal with Qdrant's multimodal semantic search.
- [Serverless Semantic Search](https://qdrant.tech/articles/serverless/index.md): Create a serverless semantic search engine using nothing but Qdrant and free cloud services.
- [Faster Disk I/O for Vector Search Using io_uring](https://qdrant.tech/articles/io_uring/index.md): Slow disk decelerating your Qdrant deployment? Get on top of IO overhead with this one trick!
- [Bulk Uploading Data to Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/articles/bulk-uploads-in-qdrant/index.md): Plan bulk uploads in Qdrant: batching, parallelization, sharding, payload indexes, quantization, and on-disk storage.
- [Question Answering with LangChain and Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/articles/langchain-integration/index.md): We combined LangChain, a modern chat model like Claude or GPT, FastEmbed & Qdrant to create a question answering system with just a few lines of code. Learn more!
- [Fine-Tuning Sparse Embeddings for E-Commerce Search | Part 4: Specialization vs Generalization](https://qdrant.tech/articles/sparse-embeddings-ecommerce-part-4/index.md): Part 4 of a 5-part series on fine-tuning SPLADE sparse embeddings for e-commerce search. Test cross-domain generalization, train a multi-domain model, and decide when to specialize vs generalize.
- [Vector Search Resource Optimization Guide](https://qdrant.tech/articles/vector-search-resource-optimization/index.md): Learn how to get the most from Qdrant's optimization features. Discover key tricks and best practices to boost vector search performance and reduce Qdrant's resource usage.
- [What is Vector Quantization?](https://qdrant.tech/articles/what-is-vector-quantization/index.md): In this article, we'll teach you about compression methods like Scalar, Product, and Binary Quantization. Learn how to choose the best method for your specific application.
- [BM42: Attention-Based Sparse Embeddings for Hybrid Search](https://qdrant.tech/articles/bm42/index.md): Introducing BM42 - a new sparse embedding approach, which combines the benefits of exact keyword search with the intelligence of transformers.
- [Enhance Search Efficiency with Binary Quantization](https://qdrant.tech/articles/binary-quantization-openai/index.md): Explore how Qdrant's Binary Quantization can significantly improve the efficiency and performance of OpenAI's Ada-003 embeddings. Learn best practices for real-time search applications.
- [Vector Similarity: Going Beyond Full-Text Search](https://qdrant.tech/articles/vector-similarity-beyond-search/index.md): Discover how vector similarity expands data exploration beyond full-text search. Explore diversity sampling and more for enhanced data discovery!
- [Filterable HNSW Without Recall Loss](https://qdrant.tech/articles/filterable-hnsw/index.md): How to make ANN search with custom filtering? Search in selected subsets without losing the results.
- [Fine-Tuning Sparse Embeddings for E-Commerce Search | Part 5: From Research to Product](https://qdrant.tech/articles/sparse-embeddings-ecommerce-part-5/index.md): Part 5 of a 5-part series on fine-tuning SPLADE sparse embeddings for e-commerce search. We packaged the entire training pipeline from Parts 1-4 into an open-source CLI and web dashboard that fine-tunes SPLADE models for any product catalog in minutes.
- [Data Privacy with Qdrant's Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)](https://qdrant.tech/articles/data-privacy/index.md): Discover how Qdrant's Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) ensures data privacy and compliance for your AI applications. Build secure and scalable systems with ease. Read more now!
- [Understanding Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)](https://qdrant.tech/articles/what-is-rag-in-ai/index.md): Explore how RAG enables LLMs to retrieve and utilize relevant external data when generating responses, rather than being limited to their original training data alone.
- [Question Answering as a Service with Cohere and Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/articles/qa-with-cohere-and-qdrant/index.md): End-to-end Question Answering system for the biomedical data with SaaS tools: Cohere co.embed API and Qdrant
- [Layer Recycling and Fine-tuning Efficiency](https://qdrant.tech/articles/embedding-recycler/index.md): Learn when and how to use layer recycling to achieve different performance targets.
- [Detecting Dataset Errors with Similarity Search](https://qdrant.tech/articles/dataset-quality/index.md): Improving quality of text-and-images datasets on the online furniture marketplace example.
- [Is RAG Dead? Why Long Context Windows Don't Replace RAG](https://qdrant.tech/articles/rag-is-dead/index.md): Uncover the necessity of vector search for RAG and learn how Qdrant empowers enterprise AI with unmatched accuracy and cost-effectiveness.
- [MUVERA: Making Multivectors More Performant](https://qdrant.tech/articles/muvera-embeddings/index.md): Multi-vector representations are superior to single-vector embeddings in many benchmarks. MUVERA embeddings aim to solve the problem of slow multi-vector search by creating a single-vector representation that approximates the multi-vector representation. This single vector can be used for fast initial retrieval using traditional vector search methods, and then the multi-vector representation can be used for reranking the top results.
- [How to Implement Multitenancy and Custom Sharding in Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech/articles/multitenancy/index.md): Discover how multitenancy and custom sharding in Qdrant can streamline your machine-learning operations. Learn how to scale efficiently and manage data securely.
- [Fine Tuning Similar Cars Search](https://qdrant.tech/articles/cars-recognition/index.md): Learn how to train a similarity model that can retrieve similar car images in novel categories.
- [Q&A with Similarity Learning](https://qdrant.tech/articles/faq-question-answering/index.md): A complete guide to building a Q&A system using Quaterion and SentenceTransformers.
- [Introducing Qdrant 0.11](https://qdrant.tech/articles/qdrant-0-11-release/index.md): Replication support is the most important change introduced by Qdrant 0.11. Check out what else has been added!
- [A Complete Guide to Filtering in Vector Search](https://qdrant.tech/articles/vector-search-filtering/index.md): Learn everything about filtering in Qdrant. Discover key tricks and best practices to boost semantic search performance and reduce Qdrant's resource usage.
- [Vector Embeddings Explained: How They Work in ML & Search](https://qdrant.tech/articles/what-are-embeddings/index.md): Discover the power of vector embeddings. Learn how to harness the potential of numerical machine learning representations to create a personalized Neural Search Service with FastEmbed.
- [Binary Quantization: 40x Faster Vector Search](https://qdrant.tech/articles/binary-quantization/index.md): Binary Quantization is a newly introduced mechanism of reducing the memory footprint and increasing performance
- [Qdrant 0.10 released](https://qdrant.tech/articles/qdrant-0-10-release/index.md): Qdrant 0.10 brings a lot of changes. Check out what's new!
- [Metric Learning for Anomaly Detection](https://qdrant.tech/articles/detecting-coffee-anomalies/index.md): Practical use of metric learning for anomaly detection. A way to match the results of a classification-based approach with only ~0.6% of the labeled data.
- [Neural Search 101: A Complete Guide and Step-by-Step Tutorial](https://qdrant.tech/articles/neural-search-tutorial/index.md): Discover the power of neural search. Learn what neural search is and follow our tutorial to build a neural search service using BERT, Qdrant, and FastAPI.
- [Understanding SPLADE and Sparse Vectors](https://qdrant.tech/articles/sparse-vectors/index.md): Learn what sparse vectors are, how they work, and their importance in modern data processing. Explore methods like SPLADE for creating and leveraging sparse vectors efficiently.
- [Product Quantization for Vector Search](https://qdrant.tech/articles/product-quantization/index.md): Discover product quantization in vector search technology. Learn how it optimizes storage and accelerates search processes for high-dimensional data.
- [Advanced Introduction to Triplet Loss](https://qdrant.tech/articles/triplet-loss/index.md): What are the advantages of Triplet Loss over Contrastive loss and how to efficiently implement it?
- [Do You Need Dedicated Vector Search?](https://qdrant.tech/articles/dedicated-service/index.md): Why vector search requires a dedicated service.
- [Scalar Quantization for Vector Search](https://qdrant.tech/articles/scalar-quantization/index.md): Discover the efficiency of scalar quantization for optimized data storage and enhanced performance. Learn about its data compression benefits and efficiency improvements.
- [Optimizing Semantic Search by Managing Multiple Vectors](https://qdrant.tech/articles/storing-multiple-vectors-per-object-in-qdrant/index.md): Discover the power of vector storage optimization and learn how to efficiently manage multiple vectors per object for enhanced semantic search capabilities.
- [Metric Learning Tips & Tricks](https://qdrant.tech/articles/metric-learning-tips/index.md): Practical recommendations on how to train a matching model and serve it in production. Even with no labeled data.
- [Minimal RAM to Serve 1M Vectors](https://qdrant.tech/articles/memory-consumption/index.md): How to properly measure RAM usage and optimize Qdrant for memory consumption.
- [Mastering Batch Search for Vector Optimization](https://qdrant.tech/articles/batch-vector-search-with-qdrant/index.md): Discover how to optimize your vector search capabilities with efficient batch search. Learn optimization strategies for faster, more accurate results.
- [Vector Search in constant time](https://qdrant.tech/articles/quantum-quantization/index.md): Quantum Quantization enables vector search in constant time. This article will discuss the concept of quantum quantization for ANN vector search.
- [Full-text filter and index are already available!](https://qdrant.tech/articles/qdrant-introduces-full-text-filters-and-indexes/index.md): Qdrant v0.10 introduced full-text filters and indexes to enable more search capabilities for those working with textual data.

## Qdrant Blog
- [Vultr and Qdrant Hybrid Cloud Support Next-Gen AI Projects](https://qdrant.tech/blog/hybrid-cloud-vultr/index.md): Providing a flexible platform for high-performance vector search in next-gen AI workloads.
